      "problem": "Find the value of $5\\,\\textrm{i} - 8\\,\\textrm{i}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To subtract two complex numbers, we just subtract the real parts and subtract the imaginary parts separately.\n\nIn this case, $5\\,\\textrm{i}$ and $8\\,\\textrm{i}$ are purely imaginary numbers. Therefore, we only need to subtract their imaginary parts, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\,\\text{i}-8\\,\\text{i}=(5-8)\\,\\text{i} & =-3\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
